      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hi -- the new \"Dog\" color filter is cool and is the most accurate version of Deuteranopia simulation present within VRChat, which is awesome! Still, I suppose this is a bump in a way to say \"hey, the original colorblindness simulation is still broken.\" \n\nThe images are as follows:\n\n1. Original, full color image\n\n2. VRChat's Deuteranopia with \"Simulate Colorblindness\" on unity-6 Build 1878\n\n3. VRChat's Dog filter\n\n4. An accurate deuteranopia shader/filter on the avatar\n\n5. Vienot 1999, another accurate colorblindness simulation, which I put the original image through\n\nI only bring this up, because again, the simulate colorblindness feature is inaccurate. The colors are almost completely inverted and desaturated from what they are supposed to be. The Dog filter is currently the best colorblindness simulation from the color filters, although I believe its inclusion is intended to be more humorous.",
